@startuml use-case
' Use cases (Claude proposal). Actors follow spec.md "Actors".
title SplitSmart - Use Cases (MVP and full product)
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Individual user" as User
actor "Group manager" as Manager
actor "Invited person" as Invitee
actor "Expense submitter" as Submitter
actor "Designated reviewer" as Reviewer
actor "Group member /\nparticipant" as Member
actor "Email service" as Mail <<system>>

Manager --|> User
Invitee --|> User
Submitter --|> Member
Reviewer --|> Member
Member --|> User

rectangle "SplitSmart - Java Swing MVP" {
  usecase "Register and verify email\n(FR-001)" as UC1
  usecase "Enroll authenticator app;\nreceive recovery codes (FR-001)" as UC2
  usecase "Sign in with password + TOTP\nor recovery code (FR-001)" as UC3
  usecase "Create group (FR-002)" as UC4
  usecase "Invite / remove member (FR-002)" as UC5
  usecase "Accept / decline invitation\n(FR-002)" as UC6
  usecase "Designate reviewer (FR-006)" as UC7
  usecase "Submit expense with split\nand optional receipt\n(FR-003, FR-004, FR-005)" as UC8
  usecase "Preview split (FR-004)" as UC8a
  usecase "Approve / reject expense\n(FR-006)" as UC9
  usecase "View notifications (FR-007)" as UC10
  usecase "View pairwise balances\n(FR-008)" as UC11
  usecase "Record payment (FR-009)" as UC12
  usecase "View summaries (FR-010)" as UC13
  usecase "Run filtered report (FR-011)" as UC14
  usecase "View expense status,\nsubmitter, outcome (NFR-004)" as UC15
}

rectangle "Full product only (not MVP)" {
  usecase "Use SplitSmart on web,\nAndroid, iOS (FR-012, NFR-005)" as UC16
  usecase "Configure multiple review\nlevels (FR-006 full)" as UC17
}

User --> UC1
User --> UC2
User --> UC3
User --> UC4
Manager --> UC5
Manager --> UC7
Manager --> UC17
Invitee --> UC6
Submitter --> UC8
UC8 ..> UC8a : <<include>>
Reviewer --> UC9
Member --> UC10
Member --> UC11
Member --> UC12
Member --> UC13
Member --> UC14
Member --> UC15
User --> UC16

UC1 --> Mail
UC5 --> Mail
UC8 --> Mail : email to signed-out members

note right of UC9
  Reviewer must not be
  the expense submitter.
end note
@enduml
